; P3: config loading and validation, ported from tests/test_config.py. The
; suite reads the two operator pages beside the model — the documented example
; and the two role blocks are load-tested rather than quoted, so a renamed key
; fails here instead of at an operator's first start — and it writes one config
; file per case, which needs Unix. Those pages are deps, so the suite runs
; against the same text a reader of the repo sees.
(test
 (name test_config)
 (libraries seekwright alcotest unix)
 (deps
  ../docs/reference/configuration.md
  ../docs/reference/deploying.md))

; P4: the provider contract's machinery — the constraint report, the caps, and
; the failure rows provider-contract.md's Failures table fixes. It reads the
; adapter sources from the sandbox as well, which is what the (deps) line is:
; the source-discipline guard is worthless if the files it scans are not inputs
; to the test, and dune would otherwise let it read a tree it did not declare.
(test
 (name test_provider)
 (libraries seekwright mcp-caps yojson alcotest)
 (deps
  (glob_files ../lib/provider.ml)
  (glob_files ../lib/provider.mli)
  (glob_files ../lib/providers/*.ml)
  (glob_files ../lib/providers/*.mli)))

